op is fine — we keep queen on c2. So we end with queen vs knight+bishop for Black?  \n\nBetter is Qxe8+ winning knight for free without losing queen: Qxe8+ K moves, then Qxa8 next move. That wins knight and rook. Yes! So sequence: Qxe8+ Kh7 (only legal), then Qxa8 (attacked by bishop c8) but bishop can take Qxa8, then we recapture with rook, winning knight and rook for bishop.  \n\nBut Qxe8+ first might allow Black to play Bxe8? No, Black can’t capture with bishop because knight blocks bishop’s diagonal to e8.  \n\nSo Qxe8+ wins knight immediately, then next move take rook.\n\nThus Qxe8+ is strong.\n\nBut is Qxe8+ in valid moves? Look at valid moves: Q: d8-e8 is there? In list: "Q: d8-e8" yes (Q: d8-e7, Q: d8-e8). So Qd8-e8 is legal (and it’s check).  \n\nSo best: Qd8-e8+.\n\nAlso consider discovered attacks: moving knight a5 somewhere to threaten something while queen on d8, but queen is hanging to bishop c8? Actually queen on d8 attacked by bishop c8? Bishop c8 attacks d8? c8 to d8 is one square diagonal? Yes bishop on c8 attacks d8 (dark square). So queen on d8 is hanging! Oh! Very important: bishop c8 attacks queen d8! So queen d8 must move or be protected. Currently queen d8 is unprotected. So top priority: save queen.  \n\nValid moves for queen d8: capture a8 or capture e8 or move to c7, d7, etc. c7 attacked by knight e8, d7 safe? d7 not attacked by any Black piece? Let’s check: d7 attacked by knight e8? Knight e8 to d6 attacks d7? No, knight e8 to d6 is one move, but knight attacks c7 and f6 and g7, not d7. Bishop c8 attacks d7? Yes bishop c8 diagonal c8-h3 covers d7. So d7 attacked by bishop c8. So queen moves to squares attacked:  \n- a8 attacked by bishop c8  \n- e8 attacked by? bishop c8 yes (e8 dark square, bishop c8 attacks e8 if knight not blocking? Actually knight e8 blocks bishop’s diagonal to e8. So e8 not attacked by bishop because knight blocks. e8 attacked by king? No. So e8 safe from capture!  \n- c7 attacked by knight e8  \n- d7 attacked by bis