l.\n\nReason: The most immediate tactical opportunity is to attack Black’s queen with Q: e8-e7, which directly threatens the queen on c7. Since the queen is undefended and there are no immediate defenders, Black will be forced to move the queen or lose it, giving White a significant material advantage. This move also centralizes the queen and prepares for further development. Other moves like developing the bishop or castling are solid but miss the chance to win material now. Therefore, the best move is to attack the queen.\n\nAnswer: Q: e8-e7"}
