hink **Q: b8-g3+** is forcing and immediately wins:  \nAfter Kh4, Q: g3-h2 threatens Q: h2-h3# next? Wait, h3 not covered yet. But K: g6-h6 or K: g6-f5 might help. Possibly easier: Q: g3-h2, Black King forced to g4/h4, then we move King to f5/g5 etc.  \nBut to avoid complications, maybe **K: g6-f7** is solid, keeping everything safe and advancing King.  \n\nHowever, with such advantage, a direct check is fine. Let’s verify mate in a few moves: from Q: b8-g3+ Kh4, then Q: g3-h2 Kg4 (only move because h5 is attacked by White King, g5 by pawn), then B: a3-d6+ (discovered check by moving Bishop) maybe leads to quick mate. So Q: b8-g3+ is good.\n\nFrom the valid moves list, **Q: b8-g3** is available. Let’s choose that.\n\nAnswer: Q: b8-g3"}
