g diagonal, eyes h6/f4 but currently not very restrictive to Black’s king.  \n4. **K: f5-g4** – Directly approaches Black’s king, but Black can move to h2 or f2 immediately. May force Black toward h1.\n\n**Reason:**  \nIn king + bishop vs king endgames, the key is to use the king and bishop together to force the opponent’s king to the board’s edge and into a corner matching the bishop’s color.  \nK: f5-g4 threatens to move closer to Black’s king on g2, and if Black moves to h2 (dark square), then our king can go to g3 or f3, with bishop possibly cutting off f2. This seems the most aggressive king move to start squeezing Black.  \n\n**Answer:** K: f5-g4'}
