anks 1-2). It’s the most “active” move that maintains central presence and pressures Black subtly, maximizing any chance Black blunders into stalemate or allows their king to be trapped near the corner later. Other moves let Black’s king advance and centralize, making any future accidental stalemate less likely.\n\n**Answer:** K: e4-d4'}
